# ---------------- WeaponData.events (Task 16 Part C: weapon & ammo data) ----------------
# Weapon definitions, data-driven. `set weapon to "Pistol"` stores the name in `my Weapon`;
# `spawn Bullet` then clones that weapon's bullet type, and `reload` uses its reload time.
# The ammo count is the actor's own `<Weapon>Ammo` variable, so two players holding the same
# pistol keep separate counts: `set ammo Pistol to 30` / `add -1 to ammo Pistol`.
#
# HOW IT LOADS: the file is read when the game loads events (and on hot reload), by name —
# WeaponData.events — before any actor's `when me appears` runs, so a weapon is complete on
# the first tick. Attaching it to a sheet is optional; the `when game starts` block below
# keeps it valid as a normal event file.
#
# BULLET TEMPLATES: `<Weapon>Bullet` names a scene actor that stages the clones, exactly like
# `spawn Bullet` does. The TK4Controls scene only ships a hidden `Bullet`, so a weapon whose
# template is missing (ShotgunPellet, UziBullet, Rocket, Grenade) warns once when it fires —
# add a hidden actor with that name to the scene when you start using it.
#
# FIELDS (per weapon, one variable each — the weapon name plus the field):
#   <Weapon>Bullet        actor template `spawn Bullet` clones while it is held
#   <Weapon>Damage        damage per hit (read by Part C.5 bullet code)
#   <Weapon>FireRate      seconds between shots
#   <Weapon>Spread        pellet spread angle in degrees (Part C.5)
#   <Weapon>Multiplier    pellets per shot (Part C.5)
#   <Weapon>Reload        seconds a `reload` takes
#   <Weapon>Sound         sound name emitted when it shoots
#   <Weapon>Smoke         particle played at the muzzle (Part C.5)
#   <Weapon>AmmoPerShot   ammo one shot spends
#   <Weapon>Ammo          ammo a fresh actor starts with
#
# Built-in defaults (code): Pistol, Shotgun, Uzi, Rocket, Grenade. Anything set here wins.

when game starts
  # --- Pistol: TK4's starting sidearm ---
  set PistolBullet to "Bullet"
  set PistolDamage to 10
  set PistolFireRate to 0.25
  set PistolSpread to 0
  set PistolMultiplier to 1
  set PistolReload to 1.2
  set PistolSound to "gunshot"
  set PistolSmoke to "muzzle"
  set PistolAmmoPerShot to 1
  set PistolAmmo to 12

  # --- Shotgun: a wide spray, slow to reload ---
  set ShotgunBullet to "ShotgunPellet"
  set ShotgunDamage to 6
  set ShotgunFireRate to 0.8
  set ShotgunSpread to 12
  set ShotgunMultiplier to 6
  set ShotgunReload to 2
  set ShotgunSound to "shotgun"
  set ShotgunSmoke to "muzzle"
  set ShotgunAmmoPerShot to 1
  set ShotgunAmmo to 8

  # --- Uzi: fast fire, short reload, little spread ---
  set UziBullet to "UziBullet"
  set UziDamage to 5
  set UziFireRate to 0.08
  set UziSpread to 4
  set UziMultiplier to 1
  set UziReload to 1
  set UziSound to "uzi"
  set UziSmoke to "muzzle"
  set UziAmmoPerShot to 1
  set UziAmmo to 40

  # --- Rocket: slow, heavy, explodes (Part C.5) ---
  set RocketBullet to "Rocket"
  set RocketDamage to 60
  set RocketFireRate to 1.2
  set RocketSpread to 0
  set RocketMultiplier to 1
  set RocketReload to 2.5
  set RocketSound to "rocket"
  set RocketSmoke to "smoke"
  set RocketAmmoPerShot to 1
  set RocketAmmo to 4

  # --- Grenade: lobbed, heavy, explodes (Part C.5) ---
  set GrenadeBullet to "Grenade"
  set GrenadeDamage to 50
  set GrenadeFireRate to 1.5
  set GrenadeSpread to 0
  set GrenadeMultiplier to 1
  set GrenadeReload to 2.5
  set GrenadeSound to "throw"
  set GrenadeSmoke to "smoke"
  set GrenadeAmmoPerShot to 1
  set GrenadeAmmo to 3
